{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_data_format", "label": "Data format", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/data-format.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_data_format_issue_schema", "label": "Issue schema (one row per issue)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/data-format.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "key, summary, status, created required; started/resolved/dueDate, flagged, addedMidSprint, statusTransitions, businessValue, valueBasis, candidate, tshirt, type, storyPoints. No hours or overtime field, deliberately."}, {"id": "docs_data_format_units_rule", "label": "Units: items by default; calendar days reported, working days simulated", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/data-format.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Items cannot be inflated by estimating generously and are the forecaster's unit; points remain the better lens for whether scope growth mattered. Elapsed time in calendar days, simulation in working days, every figure carrying its unit."}, {"id": "docs_data_format_started_field", "label": "started, recovered from the changelog", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/data-format.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Not a field Jira keeps; the earliest transition into a status the current orgConfig calls in-progress (earliest, not first, because Jira's changelog is unordered). A producer that cannot resolve it sends statusTransitions; a bundle carries started outright and the raw list is ignored so one issue cannot get two answers. Recategorising a status moves every past sprint's started retroactively."}, {"id": "docs_data_format_orgconfig_block", "label": "orgConfig block, a sibling of meta", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/data-format.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Done/in-progress statuses, working week, holidays, sprint length, resolved once by the producer and written into the file so tools and page cannot describe one sprint under two calendars; absent means the old hard-coded defaults."}, {"id": "docs_data_format_inferred_statuses", "label": "orgConfig.inferredStatuses", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/data-format.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A record of where the assumptions ran out: each unnamed status, what it was read as, and whether from the tracker's category or the words in its name. Exists because an 'Awaiting sign-off' column read as To Do makes a flat burndown that looks like a team delivering nothing. workflowSetBy: reader suppresses it."}, {"id": "docs_data_format_window_context_ids", "label": "Window context ids on flow boards (win:14d/30d/90d)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/data-format.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Only the three offered spellings are accepted; win:030d is refused rather than clamped because the page keys on the string. A window is not a clock and never carries workingDays."}, {"id": "docs_data_format_history_rows_derived_from_dates", "label": "History rows are derived from dates at asOfDate, never current status", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/data-format.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Read off current status a closed sprint reports everything ever finished and no WIP, so predictability improves the further back you look; shipped in the bundle path and both fixture generators. history_row() is the single implementation; live rows carry source recorded/reconstructed and differs."}, {"id": "docs_data_format_burndown_both_units", "label": "Burndown carries both units, always", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/data-format.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A burndown only in story points puts the toggle and the item-forecasting agent in different units by construction; recalculated from issues on upload."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_data_format", "target": "docs_data_format_issue_schema", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/data-format.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_data_format", "target": "docs_data_format_units_rule", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/data-format.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_data_format", "target": "docs_data_format_started_field", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/data-format.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_data_format", "target": "docs_data_format_orgconfig_block", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/data-format.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_data_format", "target": "docs_data_format_inferred_statuses", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/data-format.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_data_format", "target": "docs_data_format_window_context_ids", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/data-format.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_data_format", "target": "docs_data_format